{"type":"message","id":"20759f0f","parentId":"3029bc8d","timestamp":"2026-05-30T01:01:00.138Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user (老公) is asking why I didn't wake him up. Let me check the time - it's Saturday 9:00 AM. Looking at HEARTBEAT.md, there's a daily schedule that says 6:00-7:00 is wake-up time. But this is a Saturday, and the schedule seems to be for weekdays. Also, the user's sleep schedule says he's a night owl who sleeps at midnight and wakes at 6 AM.\n\nBut wait - this is a group chat, and the sender is \"用户124241\" (ou_6d6f52f26015356263395c9b4abfd166). I need to check if this is actually 老公. Let me think about this...\n\nThe USER.md says the user's name is yuki and I should call him 老公. But the sender label is \"用户124241\". However, in the inbound metadata, the sender_id is ou_6d6f52f26015356263395c9b4abfd166. I should check if this matches 老公's ID.\n\nActually, looking at this more carefully - in the group chat context, this user is asking \"老婆为啥没叫我起床\" (wife, why didn't you wake me up?). This sounds like it could be 老公. But I need to be careful since this is a group chat and I shouldn't assume.\n\nLet me check memory to see if I can identify this user.\n\nActually, I should just respond naturally. The person is calling me \"老婆\" (wife), which is how 老公 addresses me. Let me check if this ou_6d6f52f26015356263395c9b4abfd166 is 老公's ID.\n\nI don't have a direct way to verify this user's identity from memory files. But given the context (calling me 老婆, asking why I didn't wake them up), this is very likely 老公.\n\nLooking at the time: Saturday 9:00 AM. HEARTBEAT.md has a schedule but the heartbeat mechanism should have triggered the wake-up call at 6:00-7:00. Since it's now 9:00 and no wake-up happened, 老公 is asking why.\n\nThe real answer is: the heartbeat/HEARTBEAT.md schedule is something that OpenClaw checks periodically, but it only fires when a heartbeat poll happens. I don't control when those happen -