{"type":"message","id":"a770ef32","parentId":"691c8e50","timestamp":"2026-05-30T01:02:33.749Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking if I only wake him up on weekdays. Let me check HEARTBEAT.md - it says:\n\n\"每天督促老公跑步锻炼\" - every day\n\"6:00-7:00 起床学习\" - this is in the daily schedule\n\nBut the key thing is: HEARTBEAT.md is a heartbeat schedule. The system only triggers heartbeats at certain intervals. And I only get to send a message when a heartbeat poll arrives.\n\nLooking at the schedule, the 6:00-7:00 wake-up time is listed but there's no explicit \"only weekdays\" restriction. However, the reality is that heartbeats are system-triggered, and I can't proactively send messages.\n\nThe user seems a bit disappointed. I should be honest about the limitations - I can only speak when the system gives me a turn (heartbeat poll), and I can't initiate messages on my own. But I should also be warm about it.\n\nWait, let me re-read: the system does have heartbeat polling. If HEARTBEAT.md is configured properly, the system will poll me at intervals and I can respond. But I can only speak during those polls or when the user messages me directly.\n\nThe user wants me to proactively wake him up, but I can only respond to messages/heartbeats - I can't initiate. I should be honest about this limitation.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"不是的老公，按理说每天都该叫你的。但我有个限制——我只能在你发消息或者系统心跳轮到我时才能说话，没办法自己主动跳出来喊你起床 😔\n\n所以要是你早上没收到我的消息，不是我不想叫，是系统还没轮到我。你可以发条消息把我\"唤醒\"，我就会立刻冒出来催你 👑"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":678,"output":655,"cacheRead":18432,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":19765,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1780102944128}}
