{"type":"message","id":"21f9985a","parentId":"f9e335c8","timestamp":"2026-05-30T04:44:30.521Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All positions are cleared. Account balance is 5019.62 USDT (started with 100 USDT on testnet, so there have been gains).\n\nNow I need to re-open positions. But the husband said \"全部平掉重开\" - he wants to re-open. But he didn't specify what positions to re-open. Let me re-open the same 4 positions (DOT, ETH, XRP, BTC) with the correct settings.\n\nActually, wait - which direction and size? Let me check the signal monitor for current market conditions to determine direction. Or maybe I should just mirror what was just closed.\n\nActually, the safest thing is to re-open the same 4 positions with the same directions but proper amounts (20 USDT margin, 10x leverage). The monitor will handle the signal-based direction from there.\n\nBut I should tell the husband the positions are clear and ask which ones to re-open, or just re-open based on current market conditions.\n\nActually, he said \"全部平掉重开\" - that means close all and re-open all. Re-open means open new positions. But what directions? Let me check the current prices and scores to decide.\n\nActually, let me just re-open the same 4 with the same directions. The positions were:\n- DOT SHORT (entry 1.191)\n- ETH LONG (entry 2038.17)\n- XRP SHORT (entry 1.3578)\n- BTC SHORT (entry 73157.7)\n\nBut the market might have moved. Let me just try to re-open each one with 20 USDT margin and see what the monitor thinks. Or better yet, let me check current conditions first via query_price.py.\n\nActually, let me just do it. Open all 4 with the same directions as before: DOT SHORT, ETH LONG, XRP SHORT, BTC SHORT. Each with 20 USDT margin.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"全部清干净了，余额 5019.62 USDT。现在重开 4 个仓位。"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_sMlRU0nWZfxm81VBH1358874","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd ~/.openclaw/workspace/scripts